+# f09-update-report
+
+## Design
+
+- `build_plan()` now blocks existing owned symlinks, directories, and other nonregular paths, including broken symlinks, without treating them as restorable files.
+- `apply_update()` derives `missing_unchanged` from the manifest-backed plan and includes those paths in backup and write journal operations. Missing paths are recorded in `backed_up` as `null`, preserving prior absence for manual rollback; added, changed, and removed semantics remain unchanged.
+- Added `tools/smoke_core_update_missing_owned.py` with `--root`, covering exact-hash restoration, missing changed/removed paths, unrelated user-file preservation, prior-absence journal state, injected failure recovery classification, and nonregular-path blocking.
+
+## Files changed
+
+- `src/processforge_core/core_update.py`
+- `tools/smoke_core_update_missing_owned.py`
+
+## Verification
+
+- `python tools/smoke_core_update_missing_owned.py --root .` — blocked by environment `PermissionError: [WinError 5]` while creating the temporary fixture core directory; stopped per brief.
+- `python tools/smoke_core_update_manifest.py` — blocked by the same `PermissionError: [WinError 5]` during temporary fixture creation; stopped per brief.
+
+## Limitations
+
+Runtime smoke verification could not complete because the sandbox denied temporary fixture directory creation. No ACL investigation or retry variants were performed. No commits or unrelated files were changed.
